IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, sections 102 and 103 -- OFFENCES AND PROSECUTION.
-- Piece cp6, lines 2709 to 2720 of the Act file.
--
-- Section 102 makes three things offences: knowingly giving false or misleading information in an application for
-- a Social Insurance Number; knowingly applying again for a number when one has been assigned; and an employer's
-- failure to comply with section 98(5) or a regulation under paragraph 101(1)(a). Section 103 sets a five-year
-- limit for prosecuting any offence under the Act, makes an officer, director or agent of a corporation a party to
-- the corporation's offence, and applies section 41(6) to an information or complaint outside Part I.
--
-- THE SHAPE (drafting-patterns, "commits an offence"): whether conduct IS the offence is a yes/no rule over the
-- elements the section states; the penalty is a ceiling, or no ceiling, and the sentence passed is a fact about a case, never computed here.
-- Where the text states no maximum (the two summary-conviction offences of subsections 102(1) and (2) state none; the
-- Criminal Code, which would, is not among the texts this encoding reads) the answer is NOTHING, not 0.
--
-- THE JURAL RELATIONS: the Crown's power to prosecute and the person's liability to it (s 102); the person's immunity
-- once five years have run and the Crown's corresponding disability (s 103(1)); the officer, director or agent's liability
-- as a party (s 103(2)).

§ `Part III -- offences and prosecution (sections 102 and 103)`

§§ `Section 102 -- the three offences`

-- src:2709 | Offence and punishment
-- src:2710 | 102 (1) Every person who, in his application for a Social Insurance Number, knowingly furnishes any false or misleading information is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Act s 102(1) (src:2709-2710)
GIVEN `the person furnished information in an application for a Social Insurance Number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knew it was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 102(1) — the person is guilty of an offence for false or misleading information in an application for a Social Insurance Number` `the person furnished information in an application for a Social Insurance Number` `the information was false or misleading` `the person knew it was false or misleading` MEANS
        `the person furnished information in an application for a Social Insurance Number`
    AND `the information was false or misleading`
    AND `the person knew it was false or misleading`

-- "whether giving the same or different information ... and whether or not he is assigned a Social Insurance
-- Number again": neither is a condition, so neither is an input.
-- src:2711 | Idem
-- src:2712 | (2) Every person who has been assigned a Social Insurance Number and who knowingly makes application again to be assigned a Social Insurance Number, whether giving the same or different information in that application as in his previous application, and whether or not he is assigned a Social Insurance Number again, is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Act s 102(2) (src:2711-2712)
GIVEN `a Social Insurance Number has been assigned to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person made an application again to be assigned a Social Insurance Number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knew a number had been assigned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 102(2) — the person is guilty of an offence for applying again for a Social Insurance Number` `a Social Insurance Number has been assigned to the person` `the person made an application again to be assigned a Social Insurance Number` `the person knew a number had been assigned` MEANS
        `a Social Insurance Number has been assigned to the person`
    AND `the person made an application again to be assigned a Social Insurance Number`
    -- "knowingly makes application again": the person knew they were applying again
    AND `the person knew a number had been assigned`

-- src:2713 | Idem
-- src:2714 | (3) Every employer who fails to comply with subsection 98(5) or any regulation made under paragraph 101(1)(a) is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding one hundred dollars.
@ref Act s 102(3) (src:2713-2714)
GIVEN `the person is an employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer failed to comply with subsection 98(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer failed to comply with a regulation made under paragraph 101(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 102(3) — the employer is guilty of an offence for failing to require or record a Social Insurance Number` `the person is an employer` `the employer failed to comply with subsection 98(5)` `the employer failed to comply with a regulation made under paragraph 101(1)(a)` MEANS
        `the person is an employer`
    AND (   `the employer failed to comply with subsection 98(5)`
         OR `the employer failed to comply with a regulation made under paragraph 101(1)(a)`)

-- The three offences, so that the penalty rules below can be asked of each.
@ref Act s 102(1), (2), (3) (src:2709-2714)
DECLARE `cp6 Offence under section 102` IS ONE OF
    `furnishing false or misleading information in an application for a Social Insurance Number`
    `applying again for a Social Insurance Number after one has been assigned`
    `an employer's failure to comply with subsection 98(5) or a regulation under paragraph 101(1)(a)`

-- (1) and (2) are "punishable on summary conviction"; (3) is "liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- one hundred dollars". Only (3) states a maximum.
@ref Act s 102(1), (2), (3) (src:2709-2714)
GIVEN offence IS A `cp6 Offence under section 102`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 102 — the greatest fine the text states for the offence` offence MEANS
    CONSIDER offence
    WHEN `furnishing false or misleading information in an application for a Social Insurance Number` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `applying again for a Social Insurance Number after one has been assigned` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `an employer's failure to comply with subsection 98(5) or a regulation under paragraph 101(1)(a)` THEN JUST 100

DECLARE `cp6 Way an offence under section 102 is prosecuted` IS ONE OF
    `on summary conviction`

@ref Act s 102(1), (2), (3) (src:2709-2714)
GIVEN offence IS A `cp6 Offence under section 102`
GIVETH A `cp6 Way an offence under section 102 is prosecuted`
`s 102 — the way the offence is prosecuted` offence MEANS
    CONSIDER offence
    WHEN `furnishing false or misleading information in an application for a Social Insurance Number` THEN `on summary conviction`
    WHEN `applying again for a Social Insurance Number after one has been assigned` THEN `on summary conviction`
    WHEN `an employer's failure to comply with subsection 98(5) or a regulation under paragraph 101(1)(a)` THEN `on summary conviction`

§§ `Section 103 -- prosecution`

-- src:2715 | Limitation period
-- src:2716 | 103 (1) A prosecution for an offence under this Act may be commenced at any time within, but not later than, five years after the time when the subject-matter of the prosecution arose.
@ref Act s 103(1) (src:2715-2716)
GIVEN `the day the subject-matter of the prosecution arose` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 103(1) — the last day on which a prosecution for an offence under this Act may be commenced` `the day the subject-matter of the prosecution arose` MEANS
    -- "within, but not later than, five years after": the fifth anniversary is the last day (fork C6-F12 in NOTES.md: the fifth anniversary is still in time; month-end clamping as in the core's F1)
    `the date a time limit ends` `the day the subject-matter of the prosecution arose` (`a number of years` WITH `number of years` IS 5)

@ref Act s 103(1) (src:2715-2716)
GIVEN `the day the subject-matter of the prosecution arose` IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 103(1) — a prosecution for an offence under this Act may be commenced on a day` `the day the subject-matter of the prosecution arose` day MEANS
    day AT MOST (`s 103(1) — the last day on which a prosecution for an offence under this Act may be commenced` `the day the subject-matter of the prosecution arose`)

-- src:2717 | Officers, etc., of corporations
-- src:2718 | (2) Where a corporation commits an offence under this Act, every officer, director or agent of the corporation who directed, authorized, assented to, acquiesced in or participated in the commission of the offence is a party to and guilty of the offence and is liable on conviction to the punishment provided for the offence whether or not the corporation has been prosecuted or convicted.
@ref Act s 103(2) (src:2717-2718)
DECLARE `cp6 Part an officer, director or agent took in the corporation's offence` IS ONE OF
    `directed the commission of the offence`
    `authorized the commission of the offence`
    `assented to the commission of the offence`
    `acquiesced in the commission of the offence`
    `participated in the commission of the offence`
    `took none of those parts`

@ref Act s 103(2) (src:2717-2718)
GIVEN `a corporation commits an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer, director or agent of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      part IS A `cp6 Part an officer, director or agent took in the corporation's offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 103(2) — the officer, director or agent is a party to and guilty of the corporation's offence` `a corporation commits an offence under this Act` `the person is an officer, director or agent of the corporation` part MEANS
        `a corporation commits an offence under this Act`
    AND `the person is an officer, director or agent of the corporation`
    AND CONSIDER part
        WHEN `directed the commission of the offence` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `authorized the commission of the offence` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `assented to the commission of the offence` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `acquiesced in the commission of the offence` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `participated in the commission of the offence` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `took none of those parts` THEN FALSE
    -- "whether or not the corporation has been prosecuted or convicted": not a condition, so not an input.

-- Subsection 41(6) is out of range: section 41(6) (piece cp2). The substitution is of "the Department of Employment
-- and Social Development and the Minister" for "the Canada Revenue Agency and the Minister thereof".
-- src:2719 | Information or complaint
-- src:2720 | (3) Subsection 41(6) applies with respect to an information or complaint under any of the provisions of this Act other than Part I, as though for the reference therein to the Canada Revenue Agency and the Minister thereof there were substituted a reference to the Department of Employment and Social Development and the Minister.
@ref Act s 103(3) (src:2719-2720)
GIVEN `the information or complaint is under a provision of this Act other than Part I` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 103(3) — subsection 41(6) applies to the information or complaint` `the information or complaint is under a provision of this Act other than Part I` MEANS
    `the information or complaint is under a provision of this Act other than Part I`
